 since January – <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">11</span></span></code><code>]</code></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member object)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-dsc-small\">int</span> tm_year</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  years since 1900 <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member object)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-dsc-small\">int</span> tm_wday</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  days since Sunday – <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">6</span></span></code><code>]</code></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member object)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-dsc-small\">int</span> tm_yday</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  days since January 1 – <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">365</span></span></code><code>]</code></span> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member object)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-dsc-small\">int</span> tm_isdst</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  Daylight Saving Time flag. The value is positive if DST is in effect, zero if not and negative if no information is available. <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member object)</span>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-leapsecond-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-leapsecond_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Range allows for a positive leap second. Two leap seconds in the same minute are not allowed (the range <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">61</span></span></code><code>]</code></span> was a defect introduced in C89 and corrected in C99).</span>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>BSD, GNU and musl C library support two additional members, which are standardized in <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9799919799/basedefs/time.h.html\" data-external=\"1\">POSIX.1-2024</a>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-dsc-small\">long</span> tm_gmtoff</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  seconds east of UTC <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member object)</span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-dsc-small\">const char*</span> tm_zone</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  timezone abbreviation <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member object)</span>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ctime&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">tm</span> tm<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    tm.<span class=\"me1\">tm_year</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2022</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1900</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    tm.<span class=\"me1\">tm_mday</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/mktime\"><span class=\"kw1028\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mktime</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>tm<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/asctime\"><span class=\"kw1022\">std::<span class=\"me2\">asctime</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>tm<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// note implicit trailing '\\n'</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Sat Jan  1 00:00:00 2022</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/localtime\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>localtime</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  converts time since epoch to calendar time expressed as local time <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/gmtime\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>gmtime</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  converts time since epoch to calendar time expressed as Universal Coordinated Time <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/chrono/tm\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>tm</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Member objects","id":"Member_objects"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/c","title":"C Date and time utilities"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::tm","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Structure holding a calendar date and time broken down into its components."},{"label":"Member objects","children":[{"label":"int tm_sec","note":"seconds after the minute – [ 0 , 61](until C++11) [ 0 , 60](since C++11)[note 1]"},{"label":"int tm_min","note":"minutes after the hour – [ 0 , 59]"},{"label":"int tm_hour","note":"hours since midnight – [ 0 , 23]"},{"label":"int tm_mday","note":"day of the month – [1, 31]"},{"label":"int tm_mon","note":"months since January – [ 0 , 11]"},{"label":"int tm_year","note":"years since 1900"},{"label":"int tm_wday","note":"days since Sunday – [ 0 , 6]"},{"label":"+2 more"}]},{"label":"Notes","note":"BSD, GNU and musl C library support two additional members, which are standardized in POSIX.1-2024.","children":[{"label":"long tm_gmtoff","note":"seconds east of UTC"},{"label":"const char* tm_zone","note":"timezone abbreviation"}]},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"localtime","note":"converts time since epoch to calendar time expressed as local time"},{"label":"gmtime","note":"converts time since epoch to calendar time expressed as Universal Coordinated Time"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":291,"codeBlockCount":2}
